{
 "case": "P03/E02 Google × Gemini Developer API failure and truncation terminals",
 "source": "Synthetic offline fixture. Terminals follow pi-ai 0.87.1 (commit 898ab804050730e9dcefb4443875d5a932aa6a32) google-generative-ai.ts (finish reason required, error finish reasons fail after the stream with 'Provider stopped with', unknown ones throw at once) and google-shared mapStopReason; decoding and HTTP failures follow @google/genai 2.21.0 processStreamResponse ('Incomplete JSON segment at the end', the in-band error object) and throwErrorIfNotOK (JSON error bodies as sent, other bodies wrapped with status and status text). HTTP error bodies follow the Gemini API's google.rpc.Status shape.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "id": "no-finish-reason",
   "about": "The body ends without a finish reason: the open block still ends, then the call fails; the text and usage received are kept.",
   "model": "gemini-2.5-flash",
